sible waiting tiles.\n\nReason: Playing B5 preserves the most flexible hand structure with two potential pairs (T1-T1, B7-B7) and two potential chow formations (T7-T8 waiting for T6, B7-B8 waiting for B6 or B9). This maximizes my winning opportunities with 8 total unshown tiles that could complete my hand.\n\nAnswer: Play B5"}
